# Investigator authoring-mode wire permission repair

Campaign04 terminal stdout confirms stopped/failed, cleanup true, one investigator call, 2564 tokens, USD0.01921 and no candidates. Controller diagnosed the accepted actual hypothesis requesting full_source_escape against manifest.search.allow_full_source_escape false, followed by the existing author-request rejection. Campaign03+04 consumed the authorized campaign slots; no more model calls or campaign launches are part of this repair.

Changed exactly four requested files; exact preimages are under originals/, hashes in preimages.json/hashes.json, unified diff in change.patch. No evaluator closure files changed and no rebuild is needed.

wire_role_schema_v5 now accepts keyword-only allow_full_source_escape: bool | None = None. Only a canonical investigator schema together with explicit False narrows its authoring_mode enum to symbol_edits. True and None take no narrowing branch, preserving both current canonical modes. Non-bool non-None values reject. The input schema is not mutated. Existing author qualified-symbol projection is preserved.

OpenRouterOneShotJsonCompletionV5 passes its authenticated ledger manifest.search flag to the optional gateway method keyword. agent_loop passes that flag to the shared projector, while existing callers omitting it retain legacy behavior. The preparation helper passes the final manifest's same flag, so the disclosed wire body matches the actual gateway. No role-schema-authority flag is used as permission: non-author RoleSchemaAuthority.allow_full_source_escape is structurally false even when the manifest allows that mode.

Canonical request/schema authorities, historical hashes, role input classes and parsing are unchanged. The existing prospective token calculation continues to call the projector without a permission and therefore reserves the superset max(canonical, projected) size; narrowed wire does not reduce historical bounds. No global search config or forbidden-mode permission is changed. This is a generation-time schema correction; the existing local author permission rejection remains enforced if an invalid response somehow reaches it.

Actual archived campaign04 manifest SHA5fafaffb4258986fbc39c049b7d67ec4cc7804490be5a24a932ca7149ea3b561 and canonical initial schema were used for a pure local preflight. The actual false flag yields only symbol_edits; canonical/default projection retain both modes and unchanged canonical bytes. Existing superset accounting covers the actual narrowed wire. Receipt: actual-04-preflight.json. The enabled-True branch was reviewed statically only: its value cannot satisfy `is False`, so no mode narrowing occurs. No synthetic enabled cases or tests were executed.

Scoped Ruff and four-file in-memory compilation passed. No credentials, network/provider/Docker calls, synthetic probes, campaign launches, commits or hook changes. Frozen histories and global configuration remain untouched. Ready for independent review; no additional external execution is authorized.

Line-ending repair: source files themselves had no CRCRLF; the prior patch writer mixed normalized original LF with current CRLF and then Windows newline translation, causing misleading whole-file/CRCRLF patch churn. Regenerated change.patch as LF-only bytes (4011 bytes, 81 lines). Restored all unchanged source lines to exact preimage bytes, including provider.py mixed endings; inserted investigator block inherits its neighboring LF convention. No logical source line changed during repair. Other three source hashes are unchanged. provider.py final SHA58e2c114d9ad27d64f6de8b4bb318c32a620f161ec89203c249cb15d983cb1cc. Exact before/preimage/after counts are in newline-verification.json. All four compile and scoped Ruff passes; no extra blank lines or full-file semantic churn.
